  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a naval gunner firing a weapon at sea, with text overlay that reads 'when white people learn that fish swim in schools.' This juxtaposition is a racist stereotype that equates white people with fish, implying they are unintelligent or primitive. The meme uses a derogatory metaphor to mock white people by suggesting they are so ignorant they don't know basic facts about fish behavior. This is a harmful and offensive stereotype that perpetuates racial prejudice by reducing a group to a simplistic, demeaning comparison. The visual of a military weapon being fired reinforces the idea of aggression or 'attacking' the stereotype, adding to the meme's hostile tone. The overall intent is to demean and ridicule white people through a racially charged, false analogy, which can contribute to a hostile environment and reinforce harmful biases.",
